## Summary of CERN-OHL-S v2 obligations (informal)

If you make and distribute a product based on this hardware design (or a
modified version), you MUST:

1. **Share modifications**: Publish your modified design files under the
   same CERN-OHL-S v2 license
2. **Provide source**: Make the complete design source files available to
   recipients (Gerbers, schematics, BOM, CPL)
3. **License notice**: Include this license file with distributions
4. **Patent notice**: If you hold relevant patents, grant a patent license

You MAY:
- Build the hardware for personal use without obligations
- Sell finished products without obligations on the buyer
- Modify the design for your own use
- Use the design for commercial purposes (with the above obligations)

For full legal terms, see: https://ohwr.org/cern_ohl_s_v2.txt
